# Error Handling Guidelines

## Scope / Flexibility Notice
These guidelines establish consistent error handling patterns across the application. While specific error types may vary by domain, the core principles remain unchanged.

## Best Practices
- Never silently catch errors
- Use custom exception types for domain-specific errors
- Implement graceful degradation when services fail
- Log errors with appropriate severity levels
- Convert platform/framework exceptions into app-specific exceptions
- Return Result/Either types to make error handling explicit
- Implement retry mechanisms for transient failures
- Use error codes for tracking and analytics

## File / Project Structure Guidelines
- Define custom exceptions in `lib/core/error/exceptions.dart`
- Define custom failures in `lib/core/error/failures.dart`
- Implement error transformers in `lib/core/error/transformers/`
- Keep error handling logic separate from business logic
- Structure:
  ```
  lib/
    core/
      error/
        exceptions.dart
        failures.dart
        mappers/
          network_error_mapper.dart
        transformers/
          error_transformer.dart
  ```

## Coding & Styling Conventions
- Use failure classes instead of exceptions for domain layer
- Implement toString() for all error types
- Include error codes in exception constructors
- Use sealed classes for error hierarchies
- Format error messages consistently
- Differentiate between user-facing and technical errors
- Maintain exception inheritance hierarchies

## Performance & Optimization Tips
- Avoid expensive operations in exception constructors
- Don't create new exception instances for common errors
- Minimize stack trace capture for expected errors
- Use async error zones for error propagation when appropriate
- Implement circuit breaker pattern for external services
- Batch error reporting to avoid network overhead

## Testing & Validation Guidelines
- Test both success and failure paths
- Verify error transformation logic
- Mock external systems to trigger error conditions
- Test retry mechanisms and backoff strategies
- Verify error reporting/analytics integration
- Unit test custom exceptions and error handling logic
- Implement integration tests that verify error recovery
